  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "An organic compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> rotates plane-polarized light. It produces pink color with neutral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;solution. What is the total number of all the possible isomers for this compound?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> corresponds positively to neutral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> hence it will be a phenolic compound the possible structures which are optically active are as followed</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/652a092c-d682-4bc3-ac52-ca6b146603b0-image.png\"/></p><p>Hence, total optically active isomers will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
